@host = http://localhost:5238

### Is the API up, and can it reach the database?
GET {{host}}/health

### Today's sessions on the pinned clock (Friday 2026-03-06, 10:00)
GET {{host}}/api/sessions

### A day with a family cancellation after the cut-off (L005)
GET {{host}}/api/sessions?date=2026-03-03

### The exam pair as one session, and a flagged overlap (L008)
GET {{host}}/api/sessions?date=2026-03-04

### Every room (R1 to R6)
GET {{host}}/api/rooms

### Every tutor, with name and subject
GET {{host}}/api/tutors

### T1's day on the pinned clock: 7 sessions, nothing changed after the cut-off
GET {{host}}/api/tutors/T1/day

### T3's day with a tutor cancellation after the cut-off (L017)
GET {{host}}/api/tutors/T3/day?date=2026-03-05

### No such tutor (404)
GET {{host}}/api/tutors/T9/day

### Student ids are made at seed time: paste them from GET /api/sessions (attendees[].studentId)
@vuHaMy = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@tranBaoLong = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Book T2 in R4 on Saturday 13:00 (201, Location: /api/sessions/{id})
POST {{host}}/api/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tutorId": "T2",
  "roomId": "R4",
  "startsAt": "2026-03-07T13:00:00+07:00",
  "durationMin": 60,
  "studentIds": ["{{vuHaMy}}"]
}

### Into L028's room, tutor and student at once (409 with three conflicts)
POST {{host}}/api/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tutorId": "T3",
  "roomId": "R3",
  "startsAt": "2026-03-07T10:00:00+07:00",
  "durationMin": 60,
  "studentIds": ["{{tranBaoLong}}"]
}

### An 8th session for T1 on Friday (409 tutor-load)
POST {{host}}/api/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tutorId": "T1",
  "roomId": "R4",
  "startsAt": "2026-03-06T14:30:00+07:00",
  "durationMin": 60,
  "studentIds": ["{{vuHaMy}}"]
}

### Bad input: 45 minutes and no offset on startsAt (400)
POST {{host}}/api/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tutorId": "T2",
  "roomId": "R4",
  "startsAt": "2026-03-07T13:00:00",
  "durationMin": 45,
  "studentIds": ["{{vuHaMy}}"]
}

### One session (paste the id from a Location header)
GET {{host}}/api/sessions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Every rule the loaded schedule breaks (the imported week gives 4)
GET {{host}}/api/reports/violations

### Only Friday 2026-03-06 (T1's 7 sessions)
GET {{host}}/api/reports/violations?from=2026-03-06&to=2026-03-06

### Cancel one student (ids from GET /api/sessions: sessions[].id and attendees[].id)
@sessionId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@attendeeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### A family cancel (L020 at 10:30 today is chargeable: under 4 hours)
POST {{host}}/api/sessions/{{sessionId}}/attendees/{{attendeeId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cancelledBy": "family", "note": "flu" }

### A tutor cancel is never charged to the family
POST {{host}}/api/sessions/{{sessionId}}/attendees/{{attendeeId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cancelledBy": "tutor" }

### Bad input: unknown cancelledBy (400)
POST {{host}}/api/sessions/{{sessionId}}/attendees/{{attendeeId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cancelledBy": "teacher" }
